      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's an expanded and detailed summary incorporating the additional data points:\n\nThe results of the phase II clinical trial for AE-99 (Aethelgard Efficacy compound) demonstrated a statistically significant improvement in inflammatory marker levels (CRP) in 150 adults with chronic inflammation. At baseline, CRP levels were elevated across both groups, with a mean baseline level of 120.4 mg/L in the placebo group versus 115.8 mg/L in the AE-99 group. Following 12 weeks of treatment, the AE-99 group exhibited a significant reduction in CRP levels, with a mean decrease of 23.1 mg/L (p < 0.01 vs. placebo) compared to a mere 2.5 mg/L decrease in the placebo group. These findings suggest a substantial efficacy of AE-99 in reducing inflammatory markers.\n\nImportantly, the safety profile of AE-99 was generally favorable, with only a small minority of patients (3.4%) reporting nausea as an adverse event, and no serious adverse events were reported during the 12-week follow-up period. Notably, patients treated with AE-99 generally experienced a noticeable improvement in symptomatology compared to the placebo group.\n\nPlease let me know if this",
      "source": "target",
